WEBVTT


00:00:08.075 --> 00:00:10.236
Yeah!


00:00:12.279 --> 00:00:14.839
Do what you wanna do


00:00:14.915 --> 00:00:16.883
Be what you wanna be


00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.510
Freedom's no mystery


00:00:20.287 --> 00:00:22.778
Say what you wanna say


00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:24.847
Tomorrow is another day


00:00:24.925 --> 00:00:27.416
But here's the news


00:00:28.095 --> 00:00:30.154
Nobody's stopping you


00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.255
Do what you wanna do


00:00:34.635 --> 00:00:37.001
Yeah!


00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.605
Yeah!


00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.909
Hey, you just...


00:00:51.552 --> 00:00:53.019
Hi, Donny.


00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.553
Hey...


00:00:56.223 --> 00:00:57.417
Carter.


00:00:57.491 --> 00:00:59.823
Right. How much?


00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:03.991
Oh, no, no, no. No charge.
A deal's a deal.


00:01:05.132 --> 00:01:08.795
Free bait in exchange
for never having to take the bus again.


00:01:08.869 --> 00:01:10.131
Great.


00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:21.006
-Carter, talk to you for a second?
-Yeah.


00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.174
So, did he ask you
to that homecoming dance thing yet?


00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.514
Dad! Don't embarrass me.


00:01:25.586 --> 00:01:29.215
I'm your dad, it's my job.
Come home right after school.


00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:30.517
We got a lot of work to do around here.


00:01:30.591 --> 00:01:31.615
Yeah.


00:01:38.432 --> 00:01:39.956
What are you doing here?


00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:43.059
Donny's driving us until I get
my new ride. Isn't that sweet?


00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:46.333
That's sweet. There's no room for me.


00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.874
Sure there is. Come on, climb in.


00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:53.307
No, she's right. Brooke's already
wrinkling my after-lunch outfit.


00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:54.779
No, I'm not!


00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:59.308
Chelsea, this is high school, not Vegas.
You don't need a costume change.


00:01:59.386 --> 00:02:00.648
Right.


00:02:01.555 --> 00:02:02.920
But you might wanna think about it.


00:02:07.728 --> 00:02:10.788
I'm sorry, Carter.
Hey, thanks for the bait.


00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.455
-See you.
-Bye.


00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:15.866
Do what you wanna do


00:02:15.936 --> 00:02:17.904
Be what you wanna be


00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.735
Freedom's no mystery


00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:23.775
Say what you wanna say


00:02:23.844 --> 00:02:25.937
Tomorrow is another day


00:02:27.281 --> 00:02:30.409
I can't stand them.
They're such princesses.


00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.742
You said that like it's a bad thing.


00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.983
Carter, they're teenage girls.
They're probably just jealous.


00:02:37.057 --> 00:02:39.287
Yeah, I'm pretty sure they're not.


00:02:43.063 --> 00:02:45.930
It's Mason. Yes, sir.


00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:48.731
No, sir.


00:02:50.804 --> 00:02:52.237
Right away.


00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:55.602
You're leaving again?


00:02:55.676 --> 00:02:59.737
Two days, max. It's no big deal.
It's just a routine op.


00:02:59.813 --> 00:03:02.543
Yeah, that's what you always say.


00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.513
Just be careful. Okay?


00:03:07.588 --> 00:03:08.953
Always.


00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.235
You and me, pal.


00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:26.932
You and me, Dad.


00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:55.996
Her Royal Highness,
Rosalinda Marie Montoya Fiore.


00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:59.596
Princesa de Costa Luna.


00:03:59.673 --> 00:04:06.579
And you're walking, and walking as
your adoring subjects welcome you.


00:04:07.414 --> 00:04:10.542
Dimitri, my coronation
is one month away.


00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:12.608
-Why do we have to practice now?
-Ah!


00:04:12.753 --> 00:04:16.951
The rehearsal is so that
everything will be perfect.


00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:23.660
Princesa, what a beautiful
coronation dress you are wearing.


00:04:24.498 --> 00:04:27.763
Who, may I ask, designed it?


00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.699
You did, Mr. Elegante.


00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:33.137
-So I did. I am brilliant, no?
-Yes.


00:04:34.074 --> 00:04:36.474
Thank you for coming
to help Rosalinda.


00:04:36.543 --> 00:04:38.511
Now that my husband
has passed away,


00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:41.342
only she can become
queen of Costa Luna.


00:04:41.415 --> 00:04:44.009
But it is so much
for someone so young.


00:04:44.084 --> 00:04:47.417
And I'm afraid that General Kane
will take advantage of that.


00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:51.355
No, I'll be here, Sophia.
I'll protect her like she's my own.


00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:55.023
I know you will, Major Mason.
I know you will.


00:04:56.163 --> 00:04:58.131
Sounds like your music.


00:05:10.711 --> 00:05:13.839
Turn to face your subjects, Rosalinda.


00:05:13.914 --> 00:05:16.747
Honored guests, family, friends,


00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:22.016
I present to you Princesa
Rosalinda Marie Montoya Fiore,


00:05:22.089 --> 00:05:24.523
heir to the throne of Costa Luna.


00:05:24.591 --> 00:05:27.890
She is willing to be your queen.


00:05:27.961 --> 00:05:34.662
If any person has a reason to object,
let them come forward and be heard!


00:05:38.605 --> 00:05:40.163
I object.


00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:46.211
The Princesa is too young to be queen.


00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:49.476
Costa Luna and Costa Estrella
are two tiny countries


00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:53.679
who must unite and stand together
against the world.


00:05:53.754 --> 00:05:58.919
Therefore, for the good of both
our countries, l, General Magnus Kane,


00:05:58.992 --> 00:06:03.827
declare myself El Presidente
de la Republica de las Costas.


00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:06.565
Seize them!


00:06:20.714 --> 00:06:21.908
-What?
-The time is now.


00:06:21.982 --> 00:06:24.450
Go now with Major Mason. Go now!


00:06:28.255 --> 00:06:30.655
Hurry, my queen,
we must go now.


00:06:37.964 --> 00:06:39.329
Who are you?
Where are you taking me?


00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:41.390
I'm here to protect you,
but you need to trust me.


00:06:41.468 --> 00:06:42.628
But what about my mother?


00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:45.603
She's going to meet us,
but we need to hurry.


00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:57.113
-Are you all right, Mama?
-Yes, yes, darling, yes.


00:06:57.184 --> 00:07:00.176
I knew General Kane
would try something like this,


00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.948
so I made a plan to protect you.


00:07:02.022 --> 00:07:05.116
You must trust Major Mason.
You must do everything he says.


00:07:05.192 --> 00:07:06.454
Do you promise me you will do that?


00:07:06.526 --> 00:07:08.050
-Yes, Mama, I promise.
-We need to move.


00:07:08.128 --> 00:07:10.096
-Okay. Come on.
-Mama, where are we going?


00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:12.757
No, not "we," mija. You.


00:07:12.833 --> 00:07:14.892
The General will say
you abandoned the country,


00:07:14.968 --> 00:07:17.732
but I must stay, so the people know
that you will return when it's safe.


00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:19.704
No! Not without you.


00:07:22.242 --> 00:07:23.732
Here.


00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:28.304
So, no matter what happens,
you never forget you are a princess.


00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:37.354
Don't worry, mi reina bonita,
we will be together very soon.


00:07:43.063 --> 00:07:45.122
We gotta go now. Let's go.


00:08:03.917 --> 00:08:05.714
Hurry up! Inside!


00:08:10.724 --> 00:08:11.782
Go!


00:08:45.558 --> 00:08:47.788
You will never find her.


00:08:47.861 --> 00:08:51.763
And as long as she remains free,
there will be hope in Costa Luna.


00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:53.890
I could not agree more.


00:08:53.967 --> 00:08:59.166
But the Princesa is only a girl, madam.
She will contact her mother.


00:08:59.239 --> 00:09:02.174
And when she does,
I will bring her back to Costa Luna,


00:09:02.242 --> 00:09:06.144
where she will rot with her mother
in a tiny dirt cell.


00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:11.081
You will both become a tragic symbol
of futility to those who would defy me.


00:09:11.151 --> 00:09:12.743
Take her away!


00:09:46.353 --> 00:09:48.184
What is this place?


00:09:48.254 --> 00:09:49.778
You'll see.


00:10:03.103 --> 00:10:04.695
Door opening.


00:10:15.515 --> 00:10:17.210
Door closing.


00:10:22.355 --> 00:10:26.519
What... Where am l?
Is this some kind of prison?


00:10:26.593 --> 00:10:29.357
Not prison, protection.


00:10:29.429 --> 00:10:31.761
Princess Rosalinda
Marie Montoya Fiore,


00:10:31.831 --> 00:10:33.765
you are now in the safe custody


00:10:33.833 --> 00:10:38.600
of the International Princess
Protection Program, the PPP.


00:10:38.671 --> 00:10:39.933
I've never heard of it.


00:10:40.006 --> 00:10:43.965
Nobody ever hears about us
until we're needed. Good work, Major.


00:10:44.044 --> 00:10:45.102
Thank you, Director.


00:10:45.178 --> 00:10:47.043
Level three. Security.


00:10:48.515 --> 00:10:50.949
You'll be safe now, Princess.


00:10:56.156 --> 00:10:57.623
How long am I staying here?


00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:59.555
Until you're ready for stage four.


00:10:59.626 --> 00:11:02.288
Stage four? What is stage one?


00:11:02.362 --> 00:11:05.422
Extraction.
That is what brought you here.


00:11:05.498 --> 00:11:07.625
-Stage two?
- Transition.


00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:11.192
-Transition to what?
-Stage three.


00:11:11.271 --> 00:11:15.401
Come inside, why don't you?
And I will explain everything.


00:11:22.248 --> 00:11:24.773
Welcome, Rosalinda,
to the operational heart


00:11:24.851 --> 00:11:26.944
of the Princess Protection Program,


00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:31.889
a top-secret agency funded
by the world's royal families.


00:11:31.958 --> 00:11:35.792
We are actively providing protection
to 29 princesses,


00:11:35.862 --> 00:11:39.195
all of whom have been threatened
in one way or another.


00:11:40.567 --> 00:11:42.865
-Chloe, may l?
-Of course, Director.


00:11:42.936 --> 00:11:45.097
This is Princess Chandra.


00:11:45.171 --> 00:11:50.108
Last January, Major Mason rescued
her from a politically-motivated coup.


00:11:50.176 --> 00:11:53.270
We have placed her
where no one will find her.


00:11:56.249 --> 00:12:00.310
Let's just say she's a little farther north
than she's used to.


00:12:00.386 --> 00:12:03.617
-She is freezing!
-Probably. But she's safe.


00:12:04.424 --> 00:12:06.790
Let's take a walk, shall we?


00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:11.590
Please.


00:12:13.199 --> 00:12:14.723
Chloe, report.


00:12:14.801 --> 00:12:17.964
"Princess 383 has had
a successful extraction.


00:12:18.037 --> 00:12:20.733
"She arrives at 01 00 hours.


00:12:20.807 --> 00:12:25.369
"Princess 299 is still rejecting
all attempts at transformation.


00:12:25.445 --> 00:12:30.678
"And princess 107 is
in need of our services."


00:12:39.359 --> 00:12:40.986
 What about me?
Where are you sending me?


00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:45.827
Nowhere yet. First you must go
through stage three, transformation.


00:12:45.899 --> 00:12:50.598
First, we start with the hair
and then the wardrobe,


00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:53.867
until you are unrecognizable
as princesses.


00:13:02.882 --> 00:13:04.315
No! Stop!


00:13:06.986 --> 00:13:09.352
I do not know any of you people.


00:13:09.422 --> 00:13:13.256
I want to speak with Major Mason.
I only trust Major Mason.


00:13:31.611 --> 00:13:33.044
Is everything all right?


00:13:33.112 --> 00:13:35.205
Take me back to my country.


00:13:35.281 --> 00:13:38.478
Princess, I'm sorry, but General Kane
has taken control of your country


00:13:38.551 --> 00:13:40.382
and assumed command
of its government.


00:13:40.453 --> 00:13:42.648
-But I must go back.
-And you will.


00:13:42.722 --> 00:13:45.020
As soon as we find a legal way
to remove him.


00:13:45.091 --> 00:13:48.424
In the meantime,
you have to let us protect you.


00:13:48.494 --> 00:13:50.724
But what about my mother?
Who's protecting my mother?


00:13:50.797 --> 00:13:52.992
You are. As long
as you're in Princess Protection,


00:13:53.066 --> 00:13:55.591
your mom will be safe. Please.


00:13:57.770 --> 00:14:00.330
General Kane is hoping
you'll contact her


00:14:00.406 --> 00:14:02.738
so he'll know where to find you.


00:14:02.809 --> 00:14:03.901
What if he does find me?


00:14:03.977 --> 00:14:06.707
He'll make an example of you
by sending you to prison


00:14:06.779 --> 00:14:08.178
or a work farm.


00:14:08.248 --> 00:14:10.716
And Costa Luna will become
part of his own personal kingdom,


00:14:10.783 --> 00:14:14.219
with its true royal family
nothing but a memory.


00:14:15.989 --> 00:14:21.086
Bottom line, if you care about
your country, and your mom's safety,


00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:23.822
nobody can know who you really are.


00:14:31.938 --> 00:14:33.496
You may proceed.


00:14:46.886 --> 00:14:48.547
Good work.


00:14:48.621 --> 00:14:51.249
From now on,
you are no longer princess.


00:14:51.324 --> 00:14:55.420
You are now Rosie Gonzalez,
an average American girl.


00:14:55.495 --> 00:14:56.894
What happens now?


00:14:56.963 --> 00:15:00.592
-Stage four. Relocation.
-Where?


00:15:00.667 --> 00:15:02.532
Somewhere where
General Kane will never think


00:15:02.602 --> 00:15:05.833
of looking
for the Princess of Costa Luna.


00:15:08.641 --> 00:15:11.109
Welcome to Louisiana, Rosie.


00:15:44.877 --> 00:15:46.276
Over here.


00:15:57.223 --> 00:16:00.488
Welcome to your new home.
For a while, at least.


00:16:01.327 --> 00:16:03.352
Here, let me get the door.


00:16:15.508 --> 00:16:17.339
Here you go, sweetie.


00:16:19.145 --> 00:16:20.908
Thanks, Helen.


00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.813
Hey, looks like
someone's back home again.


00:16:25.418 --> 00:16:27.113
See you tomorrow!


00:16:35.728 --> 00:16:37.059
Dad?


00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:45.632
Dad?


00:16:53.546 --> 00:16:54.808
-Hello.
-Hey.


00:17:00.787 --> 00:17:03.585
-Who are you?
-Rosa... Rosie.


00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.190
Are you sure?
'Cause you don't seem sure.


00:17:06.259 --> 00:17:07.988
Rosie. I'm sure.


00:17:08.961 --> 00:17:10.758
Okay. So, what are you doing here?


00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.958
-Oh, Major Mason gave me this room.
-He did, huh?


00:17:14.033 --> 00:17:16.866
-Yes, he's been very lovely.
-Lovely?


00:17:16.936 --> 00:17:18.801
Of course, the suite is much smaller
than I'm used to,


00:17:18.871 --> 00:17:21.999
but it will feel much larger
once I have that extra bed removed.


00:17:22.074 --> 00:17:25.669
It's not extra, it's mine.
Will you excuse me for a second?


00:17:25.745 --> 00:17:27.713
Yes. You are excused.


00:17:44.997 --> 00:17:45.986
Hey, pal!


00:17:46.065 --> 00:17:47.999
Don't "pal" me.


00:17:49.101 --> 00:17:50.762
You... You met Rosie?


00:17:51.671 --> 00:17:55.163
Yeah. Who is she
and why is she in my room?


00:17:55.241 --> 00:17:59.371
Well, I had to bring her here.
The director didn't give me a choice.


00:17:59.679 --> 00:18:01.544
Okay. Just, you know, a normal dad


00:18:01.614 --> 00:18:03.673
would go to a foreign country
on a secret mission


00:18:03.749 --> 00:18:07.185
and bring his daughter back
a T-shirt, not a person.


00:18:12.992 --> 00:18:15.187
You should have warned me.


00:18:16.095 --> 00:18:19.223
Carter, I didn't have a choice.
She doesn't trust anybody but me.


00:18:19.298 --> 00:18:21.289
Yeah, I know the feeling.


00:18:21.367 --> 00:18:25.064
Hey, what I do is complicated.


00:18:26.005 --> 00:18:28.371
But if I thought for one second
it would hurt our family...


00:18:28.441 --> 00:18:30.068
Dad, I get it.


00:18:31.477 --> 00:18:33.911
-So, you're in?
-Do I have a choice?


00:18:34.614 --> 00:18:37.412
Good, 'cause I'm gonna
need your help.


00:18:37.483 --> 00:18:39.678
She needs to stay here
for a while, undetected.


00:18:39.752 --> 00:18:42.050
And in order for that to happen,


00:18:42.121 --> 00:18:44.248
she has to blend in
as a normal American teenager.


00:18:44.323 --> 00:18:47.986
Yeah, no, that's not gonna
happen, Dad. She's a princess.


00:18:49.529 --> 00:18:52.589
-Fine. Who do I say she is?
-Your cousin.


00:18:54.233 --> 00:18:57.293
Carter, thank you.
Now, if we do our job right,


00:18:57.370 --> 00:19:00.305
she'll be out of here
and back to her own country in no time.


00:19:00.373 --> 00:19:04.742
-Okay, so by Tuesday?
-lt'll be soon. I promise.


00:19:06.312 --> 00:19:08.780
-Still you and me, pal?
-No.


00:19:08.848 --> 00:19:10.645
-Come on. Come on. Come on.
-No. No. No.


00:19:10.716 --> 00:19:12.149
-ls that right? You're gonna go...
-No!


00:19:12.218 --> 00:19:13.879
-...in the water if you don't say yes.
-Put me down.


00:19:13.953 --> 00:19:16.046
-Put me down.
-All right.


00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:20.588
-You give me a headache.
-Be nice.


00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:21.649
Mmm-hmm.


00:19:31.037 --> 00:19:33.096
You have made
other sleeping arrangements?


00:19:33.172 --> 00:19:38.474
Look, the room is not yours. It's ours.
We share it.


00:19:39.111 --> 00:19:40.544
-Share?
-Share.


00:19:40.613 --> 00:19:43.173
I know that's probably
a foreign concept for a princess,


00:19:43.249 --> 00:19:46.377
but what it means is that you get
one side of the room


00:19:46.452 --> 00:19:47.714
and I get the other.


00:19:47.787 --> 00:19:49.687
So stay on your side.


00:19:57.964 --> 00:19:59.693
I don't want that.


00:19:59.765 --> 00:20:01.255
That's good.


00:20:03.502 --> 00:20:06.801
So I thought princesses
had designer clothes and stuff.


00:20:06.872 --> 00:20:09.340
Well, she had to leave all that behind.


00:20:09.408 --> 00:20:13.811
But I was thinking you could, you know,
loan her some of your stuff.


00:20:15.181 --> 00:20:17.172
Yeah, sure. Why not?


00:20:17.249 --> 00:20:20.707
Thank you. Now, go try again.


00:20:22.154 --> 00:20:25.180
-I will after this hand.
-No, now.


00:20:31.864 --> 00:20:34.128
And don't look at my cards.


00:20:45.478 --> 00:20:49.039
All right, the kitchen's closing.
Last chance to eat something.


00:20:49.115 --> 00:20:51.413
No, thank you. I wish to sleep.


00:20:52.184 --> 00:20:53.549
Okay.


00:20:54.253 --> 00:20:56.721
You may help me prepare for bed.


00:20:59.458 --> 00:21:01.551
-I "may"?
-Yes.


00:21:02.595 --> 00:21:06.122
I need a nightgown.
Preferably silk, preferably pink.


00:21:07.633 --> 00:21:10.363
Pink silk. Let me see what I've got.


00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:15.366
Here.


00:21:21.247 --> 00:21:22.271
Huh?


00:21:22.348 --> 00:21:24.179
May I use your restroom?


00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:27.151
Yeah, upstairs, first door on the right.


00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:32.617
Okay, whatever.


00:21:42.201 --> 00:21:43.793
What happened?


00:21:48.908 --> 00:21:50.773
Come on!


00:21:53.546 --> 00:21:55.810
Do they not have lizards
where you're from?


00:21:55.881 --> 00:21:59.647
Maybe, but I never see them.
That is why we have Henry.


00:22:00.519 --> 00:22:02.646
You have a royal reptile wrangler?


00:22:02.722 --> 00:22:05.850
Yes. And you should get one, too.


00:22:06.592 --> 00:22:08.116
Good night.


00:22:12.932 --> 00:22:14.559
She's gonna be okay.


00:22:14.633 --> 00:22:17.500
No. She's gonna be a royal pain.


00:22:35.821 --> 00:22:37.686
-Good morning.
-Hey.


00:22:38.858 --> 00:22:40.155
Hey.


00:22:45.831 --> 00:22:47.389
-Juice?
-Yeah.


00:22:48.868 --> 00:22:52.133
All right. There you go. Coffee done?


00:22:53.806 --> 00:22:55.034
Good.


00:22:59.245 --> 00:23:02.305
Don't be shy, Rosie.
Grab whatever looks good.


00:23:06.218 --> 00:23:08.209
-Bus is here.
-Sure you don't want a ride?


00:23:08.287 --> 00:23:10.084
Yeah, I'll be fine. You coming?


00:23:10.156 --> 00:23:13.557
-Where are we going?
-School. You're 1 6. You go to school.


00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:16.960
School. Of course.


00:23:21.333 --> 00:23:22.698
Goodbye.


00:23:31.443 --> 00:23:34.003
-Morning, honey.
-Hey, Helen.


00:23:34.079 --> 00:23:38.038
-Whoa! Who's this, now?
-That's just my cousin.


00:23:38.117 --> 00:23:40.517
-You don't say.
-Hello.


00:23:40.586 --> 00:23:42.349
Well, aren't you a cutie?


00:23:42.421 --> 00:23:43.513
I am Rosie.


00:23:43.589 --> 00:23:47.355
And I am late. Go ahead
and grab a seat, quick as you can.


00:24:06.879 --> 00:24:09.541
Call attempted.
Scrambling signal now.


00:24:09.615 --> 00:24:11.480
PPP link established.


00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:14.246
This is the director.
What is your situation report?


00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:17.619
Princess 379 is in position.
Stage four is complete.


00:24:17.690 --> 00:24:20.784
-She's safe, then?
-That's affirmative, absolutely safe.


00:24:22.027 --> 00:24:25.224
The girl can't help it


00:24:25.297 --> 00:24:28.357
The girl can't help it


00:24:28.434 --> 00:24:32.097
The girl can't help it


00:24:32.171 --> 00:24:34.002
Could this be the queen?


00:24:34.073 --> 00:24:36.268
Obviously not, Ed.


00:24:36.342 --> 00:24:37.969
Maybe this is the queen.


00:24:38.043 --> 00:24:40.773
Well, technically, no. Not yet, anyway.


00:24:40.846 --> 00:24:43.644
Nice. Honest. I like it.


00:24:46.285 --> 00:24:48.082
I'm Ed, by the way. And you're...


00:24:48.153 --> 00:24:50.121
-Rosie.
-Rosie.


00:24:50.189 --> 00:24:52.123
I'm making a documentary.


00:24:52.191 --> 00:24:55.786
Listen, "The rocky path
from humble peasant


00:24:55.861 --> 00:24:57.453
"to homecoming queen."


00:24:57.529 --> 00:25:00.157
The queen of homecoming?
What is this homecoming?


00:25:00.232 --> 00:25:02.632
You don't...
You've never heard of homecoming?


00:25:02.701 --> 00:25:04.532
No. We have no such thing
where I am from.


00:25:04.603 --> 00:25:06.332
Really? Where's that?


00:25:06.405 --> 00:25:10.535
Oh, um... That's from lowa. She's...
What are you doing?


00:25:10.609 --> 00:25:11.974
-I'm going to school.
-Bye, guys.


00:25:12.044 --> 00:25:14.103
Yes, and you're supposed to act
like a normal American girl.


00:25:14.179 --> 00:25:15.407
You're supposed to blend in.


00:25:15.481 --> 00:25:17.779
-I'm trying.
-Well, try harder.


00:25:22.321 --> 00:25:25.017
There she is, Princess Carter.


00:25:25.090 --> 00:25:27.251
-Sit down.
-Bossy, bossy.


00:25:28.360 --> 00:25:29.486
Sit.


00:25:32.464 --> 00:25:34.022
I like bossy.


00:25:36.168 --> 00:25:38.796
Excuse me, may I have this seat?


00:25:39.939 --> 00:25:41.702
I'm sorry, I think it's school property.


00:25:50.783 --> 00:25:53.013
Yeah, sure.


00:25:53.752 --> 00:25:55.617
Thank you very much.


00:25:57.022 --> 00:25:58.717
What? She's hot.


00:26:15.641 --> 00:26:20.874
This must be our new student,
Carter Mason's cousin.


00:26:53.212 --> 00:26:56.375
Where are you, my little princesa?


00:26:57.716 --> 00:26:58.774
Ah!


00:26:58.851 --> 00:27:05.051
Sophia. Thank you for joining me.
Any news from Rosalinda?


00:27:05.124 --> 00:27:06.955
No. And there will never be.


00:27:07.026 --> 00:27:10.257
Now, now, now, now.
We must not be so negative.


00:27:11.263 --> 00:27:17.065
Perhaps... Perhaps we should think
happy thoughts. Shall I begin?


00:27:17.136 --> 00:27:21.630
I am picturing
a dashing young general.


00:27:23.175 --> 00:27:26.440
And he is... He's sitting on a throne.


00:27:26.512 --> 00:27:30.209
Royal subjects shower him
with adoration.


00:27:32.351 --> 00:27:36.811
And what do you know?
They have crowned him their king!


00:27:38.023 --> 00:27:42.460
You will never be the king
of Costa Luna, not as long as I'm alive.


00:27:43.395 --> 00:27:47.229
You are ruining my happy thoughts.
Take her away.


00:27:55.774 --> 00:27:58.368
What you see is what you get
When you're looking at me


00:27:58.444 --> 00:28:01.345
I'm gonna tell it like it is
Most definitely


00:28:01.413 --> 00:28:03.938
I can tell by the way
you look me in the eyes


00:28:04.016 --> 00:28:06.382
That you're not like the other guys


00:28:06.452 --> 00:28:08.420
Hey, no cutting!


00:28:08.587 --> 00:28:10.418
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Hey!


00:28:11.356 --> 00:28:12.880
Back of the line.


00:28:12.958 --> 00:28:16.485
-Pardon?
-That's the rules. No cuts.


00:28:17.229 --> 00:28:19.493
Of course. Then I will not cuts.


00:28:19.565 --> 00:28:21.931
Hey, Rosie, come on up with me.


00:28:31.677 --> 00:28:34.305
Well? You gotta pick something.


00:28:34.379 --> 00:28:35.471
Oh!


00:28:39.485 --> 00:28:41.146
Mystery meat.


00:28:41.620 --> 00:28:44.885
Then I will have one of those.
What is it?


00:28:44.957 --> 00:28:46.481
A hamburger?


00:28:51.830 --> 00:28:52.888
Next.


00:28:53.499 --> 00:28:56.957
Am I missing
something here?


00:28:57.836 --> 00:28:59.895
Got to say the signs are clear as mud


00:28:59.972 --> 00:29:03.339
True confession.
Are you gonna eat that nasty food?


00:29:03.408 --> 00:29:06.309
When I laugh I taste the tears


00:29:06.378 --> 00:29:10.542
Sometimes I wish I'd just disappear


00:29:10.616 --> 00:29:15.280
I'm so confused, misunderstood


00:29:15.354 --> 00:29:17.185
I can't be free


00:29:17.789 --> 00:29:21.782
Is it just me who feels this way?


00:29:21.860 --> 00:29:26.354
Trying to be where I am
So out of place


00:29:26.431 --> 00:29:30.663
Can't I just wait to see what's right?


00:29:31.069 --> 00:29:35.563
'Cause it looks like
we're all just flying blind


00:29:36.475 --> 00:29:39.239
Check her out.
Who does she think she is?


00:29:40.112 --> 00:29:42.910
I know. She thinks
she's Carter's cousin.


00:29:50.189 --> 00:29:51.281
Ow!


00:29:51.356 --> 00:29:54.382
Oh, was that your leg? I'm sorry.


00:29:55.627 --> 00:29:58.152
She may be a loser like her cousin,
but she's dangerous.


00:29:58.230 --> 00:30:01.495
-Really? Why?
-Are you serious? Look at her.


00:30:01.567 --> 00:30:04.127
I know. Totally love the hair.


00:30:05.337 --> 00:30:06.429
Ow!


00:30:11.710 --> 00:30:12.938
What are you doing?


00:30:13.011 --> 00:30:15.878
Eating a hamburger.
Have you ever tried one?


00:30:15.948 --> 00:30:18.815
Yes. And FYl,
they have hamburgers in lowa.


00:30:19.585 --> 00:30:20.574
Oh!


00:30:21.119 --> 00:30:22.347
Right.


00:30:22.921 --> 00:30:25.981
-You're supposed to be blending in.
-I am blending.


00:30:26.058 --> 00:30:28.083
Speaking fluent French in class?


00:30:28.160 --> 00:30:31.061
And eating hamburger
like you're having tea with the Queen?


00:30:31.129 --> 00:30:34.690
-Well, how else should it be eaten?
-Like this.


00:30:36.602 --> 00:30:38.069
The works.


00:30:39.805 --> 00:30:41.534
There you go.


00:30:42.574 --> 00:30:43.939
Mmm-hmm.


00:30:46.878 --> 00:30:48.402
Stop.


00:30:51.984 --> 00:30:53.212
Now.


00:30:56.355 --> 00:30:58.084
-Like this?
-It's perfect.


00:30:58.156 --> 00:31:00.386
Can I have your attention, please?
I have an announcement to make.


00:31:00.459 --> 00:31:03.189
Can we sit down
and settle down, please?


00:31:04.029 --> 00:31:06.725
On Monday,
we'll be taking nominations


00:31:06.798 --> 00:31:08.129
for the homecoming court.


00:31:09.334 --> 00:31:12.633
These nominees must be girls
of exemplary character.


00:31:12.704 --> 00:31:16.105
Kind, intelligent,
honest, charitable members


00:31:16.174 --> 00:31:17.835
of the Lake Monroe community.


00:31:17.909 --> 00:31:20.377
Now, the three girls
with the most votes


00:31:20.445 --> 00:31:23.380
will become
your homecoming princesses.


00:31:26.251 --> 00:31:28.515
There's more, there's more.


00:31:28.587 --> 00:31:31.181
On Friday night, at our annual dance,


00:31:31.256 --> 00:31:33.690
one of these lucky girls
will be crowned


00:31:33.759 --> 00:31:36.922
your homecoming queen
of Lake Monroe High.


00:31:36.995 --> 00:31:38.223
Yeah!


00:31:38.764 --> 00:31:40.231
Thank you.


00:31:42.467 --> 00:31:44.230
You vote for royalty here?


00:31:44.303 --> 00:31:46.533
We're a democracy. We're into voting.


00:31:46.605 --> 00:31:51.133
So then, anyone can be a princess?
Even you?


00:31:52.678 --> 00:31:54.305
Theoretically.


00:31:56.581 --> 00:31:59.106
Excuse me, everyone.
May I have your attention?


00:31:59.184 --> 00:32:01.015
-What are you doing? Sit down!
-No, no.


00:32:01.086 --> 00:32:05.022
I would like to nominate my cousin,
Carter Mason, to be your queen.


00:32:05.991 --> 00:32:09.154
I think that she would
make an excellent ruler.


00:32:10.762 --> 00:32:12.093
Carter?


00:32:13.665 --> 00:32:15.064
Yeah, right.


00:32:15.834 --> 00:32:19.930
-Carter. Carter!
-Carter? That's hilarious.


00:32:20.238 --> 00:32:22.297
Was that for real? Wow!


00:32:23.575 --> 00:32:24.769
Oh, man.


00:32:24.976 --> 00:32:27.001
Looks like I'm the queen.


00:32:28.980 --> 00:32:30.242
Carter!


00:32:31.483 --> 00:32:33.781
-Carter!
-Leave me alone.


00:32:33.852 --> 00:32:35.717
I order you to stop.


00:32:37.222 --> 00:32:39.850
You order me? You order me.


00:32:39.925 --> 00:32:42.450
I order you to take a long walk
off a short pier.


00:32:42.527 --> 00:32:44.290
You cannot order me to do anything.


00:32:44.363 --> 00:32:45.796
Wanna bet?
You're in my kingdom now.


00:32:45.864 --> 00:32:47.729
Okay, hey, hey, hey. Whoa, whoa.


00:32:47.866 --> 00:32:48.890
Whoa, what's going on?


00:32:48.967 --> 00:32:51.936
Dad, she can't do it.
She can't act normal.


00:32:52.371 --> 00:32:54.430
-I am normal.
-Really? Okay.


00:32:54.506 --> 00:32:57.532
So, a normal person who has
never seen a hamburger before


00:32:57.609 --> 00:32:59.474
can order one in six languages?


00:32:59.544 --> 00:33:00.841
Really? You did that?


00:33:00.912 --> 00:33:02.743
I always speak to my staff
in their native tongue.


00:33:02.814 --> 00:33:05.476
They're not your staff.
They're lunch ladies, okay?


00:33:05.550 --> 00:33:07.279
Dad, can't you see
that this isn't gonna work?


00:33:07.352 --> 00:33:11.482
Carter, it's gonna work, okay?
We just have to give it a little time.


00:33:17.929 --> 00:33:19.396
It'll work.


00:33:54.933 --> 00:33:57.902
It's gonna be a scorcher again today...


00:33:58.036 --> 00:33:59.025
-Hey, Ernie.
-Hi, Carter.


00:33:59.104 --> 00:34:00.799
-Hello.
-Oh, great.


00:34:00.872 --> 00:34:03.773
Good morning, Carter.
What are you doing?


00:34:03.842 --> 00:34:05.139
Chores.


00:34:05.877 --> 00:34:09.904
-Chores? I do not understand.
-No, of course not.


00:34:10.749 --> 00:34:14.207
Perhaps I could learn this "chores."
You could teach me.


00:34:15.587 --> 00:34:18.215
You know, that's the best idea
you've had.


00:34:18.290 --> 00:34:19.621
What must I do?


00:34:19.691 --> 00:34:22.319
We'll start you off easy. Inventory.


00:34:22.394 --> 00:34:24.555
-lnventory?
-Counting.


00:34:26.331 --> 00:34:32.270
You count what's in here,
and put it in here. Have fun.


00:34:33.071 --> 00:34:37.269
Oh! And when you're done,
there's a whole other shelf, too.


00:34:56.962 --> 00:34:57.951
One.


00:35:00.499 --> 00:35:03.900
-Everything okay?
-Yeah. Just peachy.


00:35:05.437 --> 00:35:07.405
-You got the bow?
-Uh-huh.


00:35:07.472 --> 00:35:08.734
Stay above that line.


00:35:08.807 --> 00:35:10.741
-What line?
-Right there.


00:35:10.809 --> 00:35:12.003
Okay.


00:35:21.219 --> 00:35:24.245
Carter, what's Rosie doing
in the bait shop?


00:35:24.322 --> 00:35:25.755
Chores.


00:35:27.359 --> 00:35:28.417
Dad.


00:35:29.361 --> 00:35:30.555
Rosie!


00:35:31.296 --> 00:35:34.390
-Are you okay?
-I'm all right.


00:35:36.034 --> 00:35:38.059
I think I need to bathe.


00:35:41.773 --> 00:35:44.742
Carter, why don't you go on
in and clean this up, okay?


00:35:45.343 --> 00:35:49.245
-Why me? She's the one who did it.
-Come on, pal. I'll help you.


00:35:49.314 --> 00:35:52.215
-All right, it... It's not funny.
-Yes. Come on.


00:35:52.284 --> 00:35:53.979
-You know it's a little funny.
-All right. Here. Go.


00:35:54.052 --> 00:35:55.519
-You wanna laugh, too.
-No, I don't wanna laugh.


00:35:55.587 --> 00:35:56.986
-Yes, you do.
-This is serious. Come on.


00:35:59.024 --> 00:36:01.254
-What do you want for dinner tonight?
-Pizza.


00:36:01.326 --> 00:36:05.194
Pizza? We had pizza last night.
How about... How about burgers?


00:36:05.263 --> 00:36:07.629
How about this? Pizza and burgers.


00:36:08.300 --> 00:36:09.699
-Pizza and burgers.
-Yeah. I wanna do both.


00:36:09.768 --> 00:36:13.169
-One as an appetizer, or just together?
-I don't know.


00:36:17.375 --> 00:36:20.435
I didn't know we still had all that stuff.


00:36:20.512 --> 00:36:23.037
-What's all this?
-A proper dinner.


00:36:23.114 --> 00:36:24.581
To thank you for helping me
clean up the mess


00:36:24.649 --> 00:36:26.844
that I made in your shop of bugs.


00:36:26.918 --> 00:36:28.749
-It's bait.
-I'm aware.


00:36:29.154 --> 00:36:30.246
Okay.


00:36:33.892 --> 00:36:35.883
-Here. Let me.
-No, no.


00:36:35.961 --> 00:36:38.589
Thank you, but tonight, I serve you.


00:36:38.663 --> 00:36:41.359
Well, I'm not gonna say no to that.


00:36:41.600 --> 00:36:42.658
It is for you.


00:36:42.734 --> 00:36:44.133
-For me?
-Mmm-hmm.


00:36:44.202 --> 00:36:46.830
To wear. Okay. Fine.


00:36:48.807 --> 00:36:50.536
Come on, Carter.


00:36:52.911 --> 00:36:56.779
So, you cook?
I thought you had servants for that.


00:36:56.848 --> 00:36:58.440
Actually, my mother grew up a peasant.


00:36:59.851 --> 00:37:02.115
So she taught me many family recipes.


00:37:11.596 --> 00:37:12.620
Wow!


00:37:12.697 --> 00:37:14.528
Yeah, that sounds kind of fancy.


00:37:14.599 --> 00:37:18.194
-Why don't we just order pizza?
-No, it's chicken and rice.


00:37:18.269 --> 00:37:20.567
Fantastic. Bring it on, Rosie.


00:37:22.040 --> 00:37:24.702
You know, I haven't had
a real home-cooked meal since...


00:37:24.776 --> 00:37:26.175
Forever.


00:37:27.278 --> 00:37:28.575
Right.


00:37:29.414 --> 00:37:31.041
Let's dig in!


00:37:34.085 --> 00:37:35.450
-How do you like it?
-That...


00:37:35.520 --> 00:37:38.683
That is really, really good.
Gee, I had no idea you can cook.


00:37:38.757 --> 00:37:41.885
-Thank you.
-This is terrific. You're wonderful.


00:37:42.794 --> 00:37:45.194
Thank you. Would you like a roll?


00:37:45.263 --> 00:37:47.094
-You made rolls, too?
-Yes.


00:37:47.165 --> 00:37:49.360
-I had no idea.
-Yes.


00:37:50.468 --> 00:37:51.457
Wow!


00:37:51.770 --> 00:37:54.500
Must be nice to play peasant for a day.


00:37:58.877 --> 00:38:00.777
Would you excuse me?


00:38:29.607 --> 00:38:31.802
You do not know me, Carter.


00:38:33.511 --> 00:38:34.944
What's the big deal?


00:38:35.013 --> 00:38:36.878
You'll be back with your servants


00:38:36.948 --> 00:38:40.543
and your personal chef
and private tutors soon enough.


00:38:44.723 --> 00:38:47.487
How much did your father
tell you about me?


00:38:47.559 --> 00:38:50.528
Other than the obvious,
I think we're on a need-to-know basis.


00:38:50.595 --> 00:38:55.658
I think you need to know that my name
is Rosalinda Marie Montoya Fiore,


00:38:55.734 --> 00:38:58.794
-and I am a royal princess.
-No kidding.


00:38:58.870 --> 00:39:02.135
I am from a small island nation
called Costa Luna.


00:39:02.207 --> 00:39:05.176
-Never heard of it.
-lt is not on most maps.


00:39:05.477 --> 00:39:09.072
It is very small,
very unimportant to large countries,


00:39:09.147 --> 00:39:11.638
but very important to me.


00:39:23.261 --> 00:39:26.128
When my father died,
he left Costa Luna to me.


00:39:30.435 --> 00:39:31.595
You don't have to tell me...


00:39:31.669 --> 00:39:35.036
One month before my coronation,
our palace was attacked.


00:39:35.106 --> 00:39:38.701
Your father was very brave.


00:39:38.777 --> 00:39:40.768
He risked his life for you, I know.


00:39:40.845 --> 00:39:44.474
That's his job. He rescues
poor, oppressed princesses.


00:39:45.717 --> 00:39:48.948
Did he tell you we had
to leave my mother behind?


00:39:49.020 --> 00:39:52.854
The man who invaded Costa Luna
now holds her as a hostage.


00:39:54.893 --> 00:39:55.917
I didn't know.


00:39:55.994 --> 00:39:57.655
They told me
my becoming Rosie Gonzalez


00:39:57.729 --> 00:39:59.754
was the only way to keep her safe.


00:39:59.831 --> 00:40:01.799
Stop. It's okay.


00:40:01.866 --> 00:40:05.825
Carter, whatever I did to make
you dislike me, I am truly sorry.


00:40:05.904 --> 00:40:10.603
I will try to blend in.
I will try to be from lowa.


00:40:13.011 --> 00:40:16.003
It is the only way
to save my mother's life.


00:40:20.585 --> 00:40:22.553
Let's just start over.


00:40:23.555 --> 00:40:25.352
I would like that.


00:40:25.423 --> 00:40:28.153
But you need to lighten up
on this princess stuff.


00:40:28.226 --> 00:40:29.488
It's really annoying.


00:40:29.561 --> 00:40:34.294
Absolutely. Please, I only want
to be this typical American teenager.


00:40:35.433 --> 00:40:38.459
You know what?
I think we can arrange that.


00:40:44.409 --> 00:40:46.809
I love this place! What is it?


00:40:47.512 --> 00:40:50.379
It's a bowling alley. That's bowling.


00:40:50.448 --> 00:40:54.544
Just do what I do and don't draw
any attention to yourself, please.


00:40:54.619 --> 00:40:55.881
Right.


00:41:00.091 --> 00:41:01.854
-Thank you.
-Sure.


00:41:03.428 --> 00:41:05.862
-Carter! How you doing?
-Hi, Ed.


00:41:05.930 --> 00:41:09.161
-Hi. How you doing, Rosie?
-I'm well, thank you.


00:41:10.134 --> 00:41:12.728
-What'll it be?
-Bowling, please.


00:41:12.804 --> 00:41:14.396
No kidding.


00:41:17.542 --> 00:41:19.635
Five-and-a-half coming up.


00:41:20.511 --> 00:41:22.274
-Thank you.
-Sure.


00:41:24.849 --> 00:41:27.010
-What size?
-Excuse me?


00:41:27.752 --> 00:41:29.982
Your feet. What size?


00:41:31.122 --> 00:41:34.114
I do not know.
All of my shoes are made for me.


00:41:34.192 --> 00:41:36.786
There's a shock.
Just get her some shoes.


00:41:36.861 --> 00:41:38.192
Okay.


00:42:00.385 --> 00:42:01.875
Your Highness.


00:42:02.954 --> 00:42:04.819
Why, thank you, Edward.


00:42:05.823 --> 00:42:10.283
-It's Edwin, actually.
-Edwin. That is a wonderful name.


00:42:10.361 --> 00:42:14.559
Thank you. It's been
a pleasure serving you, milady.


00:42:14.632 --> 00:42:16.827
All right. Thank you, Romeo.


00:42:17.635 --> 00:42:18.829
Okay.


00:42:19.771 --> 00:42:22.239
You're not blending in. Pick a ball.


00:42:22.307 --> 00:42:23.399
Did you see that?


00:42:23.474 --> 00:42:27.535
-Yeah. Nobody ever does that for us.
-They do now.


00:42:29.981 --> 00:42:32.916
-Your shoe's untied.
-Don't trip.


00:42:39.223 --> 00:42:40.315
Oh!


00:42:42.694 --> 00:42:44.286
Careful there.


00:42:50.735 --> 00:42:53.363
Donny, you don't have
to carry that for her.


00:42:53.438 --> 00:42:56.168
She can do it herself
like a normal person.


00:42:56.240 --> 00:42:59.573
-So I'll just take this.
-Whatever you say...


00:43:01.145 --> 00:43:03.443
-Carter.
-Right.


00:43:08.152 --> 00:43:12.054
-So, Donny is your boyfriend?
-What? No, no. He's just a friend.


00:43:12.123 --> 00:43:14.148
But he is very special to you.


00:43:14.225 --> 00:43:18.423
I see the way you look at him.
It's the same way that Ed looks at you.


00:43:19.097 --> 00:43:22.931
Okay, you're obviously not from here,
so just bowl. You first.


00:43:23.901 --> 00:43:25.630
How do I win?


00:43:25.703 --> 00:43:28.797
You win by knocking down
those white pins.


00:43:29.540 --> 00:43:31.371
Okay, I'm ready.


00:43:33.044 --> 00:43:36.172
-What?
-You may fire at the target.


00:43:37.615 --> 00:43:39.640
You may fire it yourself.


00:43:57.769 --> 00:43:59.327
Impossible.


00:44:00.571 --> 00:44:02.300
Nice shot, Rosie!


00:44:21.526 --> 00:44:23.255
You done already, Carter?


00:44:23.327 --> 00:44:26.228
Yeah. Our lane's
getting a little crowded.


00:44:29.300 --> 00:44:32.269
You don't really like your cousin,
do you?


00:44:32.336 --> 00:44:39.105
No, it's... It's just...
She can be sometimes, you know, a...


00:44:39.177 --> 00:44:41.372
Princess. She could win it all.


00:44:41.446 --> 00:44:43.437
She is getting really popular.


00:44:43.514 --> 00:44:47.280
The vote is on Monday. We can't
let her get more popular than we are.


00:44:47.351 --> 00:44:50.718
There's only one thing to do
in a situation like this.


00:44:50.788 --> 00:44:56.124
Excuse me! Excuse me! Roe!
Excuse me! Excuse me! Roe.


00:44:56.194 --> 00:44:59.857
You are such a natural.
Will you show us how to bowl like that?


00:44:59.931 --> 00:45:04.834
-Of course. But my name is Rosie.
-Oh! Roe's our nickname we gave you.


00:45:04.902 --> 00:45:07.393
We give all of our friends nicknames.
She's Chels.


00:45:07.472 --> 00:45:11.135
And she's Brookie and you're Roe.
You're one of us now.


00:45:16.247 --> 00:45:17.976
Carter?
What?


00:45:18.049 --> 00:45:20.517
Why do you care so much
for this boy Donny?


00:45:20.585 --> 00:45:22.416
Who says I care for him?


00:45:24.889 --> 00:45:28.552
Fine. I've been totally in love with him
since, like, the third grade,


00:45:28.626 --> 00:45:30.093
when he kissed me
under the basketball hoop.


00:45:30.161 --> 00:45:32.527
-ls that what you want to hear?
-He is quite beautiful.


00:45:32.597 --> 00:45:34.394
Much like a prince.


00:45:35.099 --> 00:45:38.296
I wonder if he is
beautiful on the inside as well.


00:45:39.971 --> 00:45:44.340
-Shall we bowl again tomorrow?
-I can't. I'm working at the bait shack.


00:45:44.609 --> 00:45:46.372
I've never worked before.
Is this normal?


00:45:46.444 --> 00:45:48.605
Yes. Lots of kids have jobs.


00:45:48.679 --> 00:45:50.772
-Then I will help you.
-You can't.


00:45:50.848 --> 00:45:52.509
-Why not?
-Because it's mine.


00:45:52.583 --> 00:45:55.313
You can't have everything that's mine!


00:45:55.386 --> 00:45:59.152
Well, just... Want a job so bad?
Just go get one yourself.


00:46:01.592 --> 00:46:02.923
All right.


00:46:05.563 --> 00:46:07.326
Good night, Carter.


00:46:22.513 --> 00:46:24.208
Thank you
for giving me this job, Chelsea.


00:46:24.282 --> 00:46:27.843
No prob, Roe. Daddy owns,
like, 17 Udderlys all over the South.


00:46:27.919 --> 00:46:30.717
-He's the King.
-Your father is a king?


00:46:30.788 --> 00:46:33.723
Of frozen yogurt. One more thing.


00:46:35.793 --> 00:46:37.658
You have to wear this.


00:46:45.770 --> 00:46:47.670
So these are
the frozen yogurt machines.


00:46:47.738 --> 00:46:49.205
You just pull the lever
and when it comes out


00:46:49.273 --> 00:46:51.332
you just put a little swirly on top
and you're good to go, okay?


00:46:51.409 --> 00:46:53.309
-Swirly?
-This is gonna be great.


00:46:53.377 --> 00:46:55.140
And all your friends
will be here to support you.


00:46:55.213 --> 00:46:57.875
We all want you to succeed
at your first job.


00:46:57.949 --> 00:46:59.883
-Thank you so much.
-Uh-huh.


00:47:25.409 --> 00:47:26.569
Ed!


00:47:27.378 --> 00:47:29.005
Here she is, folks,


00:47:29.080 --> 00:47:33.107
a future homecoming princess
of Lake Monroe, Louisiana.


00:47:33.184 --> 00:47:35.311
Who is this natural beauty, you ask?


00:47:35.386 --> 00:47:37.251
Will you go away? I'm working.


00:47:37.321 --> 00:47:40.552
This is Carter Mason.


00:47:40.625 --> 00:47:42.855
Secret identity? Bait Girl.


00:47:42.927 --> 00:47:44.758
So confident of her innate royalty,


00:47:44.829 --> 00:47:49.129
she is completely unafraid to handle
whatever disgusting creature...


00:47:49.200 --> 00:47:50.258
Hey!


00:47:50.334 --> 00:47:52.962
Isn't that... Not on my camera, please.


00:47:53.037 --> 00:47:54.231
Then turn it off.


00:47:54.305 --> 00:47:55.397
No.


00:47:55.473 --> 00:47:57.805
Today's my last day
to get the "before" footage.


00:47:57.875 --> 00:47:59.274
The princess vote is tomorrow.


00:47:59.343 --> 00:48:01.311
Well, then go shoot Chelsea or Brooke.


00:48:01.379 --> 00:48:04.143
Nah. I've got tons of them already.


00:48:04.215 --> 00:48:06.547
-They pay me to film them.
-ls that why you're doing this?


00:48:06.617 --> 00:48:08.881
-'Cause of the money?
-Absolutely.


00:48:08.953 --> 00:48:11.547
I'm the only senior guy in Lake Monroe
who doesn't have a car.


00:48:11.622 --> 00:48:12.850
Figures.


00:48:15.226 --> 00:48:17.558
You really hate
this whole princess thing, don't you?


00:48:17.628 --> 00:48:21.120
I don't hate it exactly.
I just think it's shallow.


00:48:21.198 --> 00:48:24.429
Girls like Chelsea and Brooke,
all they care about is shoes.


00:48:24.502 --> 00:48:27.903
Like wearing the right clothes
makes them superior.


00:48:27.972 --> 00:48:30.304
I just want to do something
more important with my life,


00:48:30.374 --> 00:48:31.807
Iike my dad.


00:48:32.743 --> 00:48:35.803
Yeah, yeah,
he does sell some sick bait.


00:48:36.614 --> 00:48:37.672
Right.


00:48:37.748 --> 00:48:40.683
So, speaking of princesses,
where's Rosie?


00:48:41.752 --> 00:48:42.741
How should I know?


00:48:48.626 --> 00:48:50.617
I think I just found her.


00:48:51.962 --> 00:48:54.522
Hey, I've been waiting here
for, like, 10 minutes.


00:48:54.965 --> 00:48:57.058
I haven't got all day!


00:48:57.868 --> 00:48:59.358
Just a second.


00:49:07.378 --> 00:49:08.709
Hold on.


00:49:09.480 --> 00:49:10.469
Oh, no!


00:49:16.187 --> 00:49:18.052
It's not brain science!


00:49:18.122 --> 00:49:19.851
Come on,
what are they paying you for?


00:49:19.924 --> 00:49:22.358
I've been waiting for, like, ever!


00:49:24.495 --> 00:49:28.761
Come on, Chels.
She's dying in there. Help her out.


00:49:29.633 --> 00:49:32.898
You're absolutely right.
Brookie, we should go in there.


00:49:32.970 --> 00:49:35.768
Oh, Chels.
If only our pedicures were dry.


00:49:40.311 --> 00:49:41.437
Fine.


00:49:42.079 --> 00:49:45.048
Bull, will you do me a huge favor?


00:49:45.649 --> 00:49:47.116
Yeah. Yeah.


00:49:53.124 --> 00:49:55.991
Wait.
How do I know it's the right one?


00:49:56.260 --> 00:49:59.024
It's big. It's red. Can't miss it.


00:50:14.078 --> 00:50:16.603
I can't believe it.
This is ridiculous!


00:50:16.680 --> 00:50:20.116
I want my yogurt, okay?
You need some help, or what?


00:50:22.586 --> 00:50:23.575
Hello?


00:50:24.722 --> 00:50:26.189
I have to go!


00:50:41.772 --> 00:50:43.205
Oh, no!


00:51:15.372 --> 00:51:16.805
What are you doing?


00:51:16.874 --> 00:51:19.172
Are you okay? Come here, Rosie.


00:51:21.245 --> 00:51:25.341
-You said to get a job.
-Not this one! This job's for losers.


00:51:25.416 --> 00:51:28.283
Trust me, I've had this job.
The bait shop is a step up.


00:51:29.954 --> 00:51:31.785
Hey, check it out.


00:51:36.760 --> 00:51:39.923
-What is happening?
-Chelsea set you up.


00:51:39.997 --> 00:51:44.195
She invited all those people to come
watch you make a fool of yourself.


00:51:44.268 --> 00:51:46.133
Carter, it's okay.


00:51:47.304 --> 00:51:48.635
I am not a fool.


00:51:48.706 --> 00:51:51.539
And she cannot make something
out of me that I am not.


00:51:51.609 --> 00:51:53.907
Rosie, we have to do something.


00:51:55.145 --> 00:51:59.206
I will turn the other cheek,
because that is what princesses do.


00:52:25.409 --> 00:52:27.843
Your father, the King of Yogurts,


00:52:28.879 --> 00:52:31.404
would be very disappointed in you.


00:52:44.028 --> 00:52:46.496
Yeah, well, I'm not a princess.


00:52:55.472 --> 00:52:56.996
She can't be a princess!


00:52:57.074 --> 00:52:59.065
Don't freak, but she kind of can.


00:52:59.143 --> 00:53:01.475
I've just been texted, like, 1 0 times.


00:53:01.545 --> 00:53:03.570
Everybody thinks she's pretty cool.


00:53:03.647 --> 00:53:06.445
Tomorrow, when the whole school
votes for three princesses,


00:53:06.517 --> 00:53:08.576
she could be one of them.


00:53:08.652 --> 00:53:10.984
-And if she gets enough votes...
-Don't say it.


00:53:11.055 --> 00:53:12.249
...she could become queen.


00:53:12.323 --> 00:53:14.848
No, I'm the queen! It's my destiny!


00:53:16.927 --> 00:53:18.724
That's kind of iffy now.


00:53:18.796 --> 00:53:22.095
I'd rather eat carbs than see her
wearing my crown.


00:53:22.533 --> 00:53:24.558
-We have to stop her.
-How?


00:53:26.003 --> 00:53:30.030
If she never becomes a princess,
she can't be the queen, right?


00:53:30.574 --> 00:53:32.838
I'm not sure where you're going here.


00:53:32.910 --> 00:53:36.607
Grab your cell.
We've got a whole lot of texting to do.


00:53:39.483 --> 00:53:41.781
So, it's a skill that most Americans
master in, like, the third grade,


00:53:41.852 --> 00:53:44.821
-but it's never too late to learn.
-I am ready to try.


00:53:44.888 --> 00:53:46.219
Good luck.


00:53:52.162 --> 00:53:53.390
Nice.


00:53:53.897 --> 00:53:58.493
Okay, next we'll work on slouching,
eye-rolling and talking back to my dad.


00:53:58.736 --> 00:54:02.467
If Mr. Elegante could see me right now,
he would be so mad at me.


00:54:02.539 --> 00:54:05.531
-Who's Mr. Elegante?
-My royal dress designer.


00:54:06.010 --> 00:54:07.500
You're kidding, right?


00:54:07.578 --> 00:54:09.808
No. He is a close family friend.


00:54:09.880 --> 00:54:13.577
If there were ever an emergency,
he would be the first I would call.


00:54:14.118 --> 00:54:16.211
Must be nice to be a queen.


00:54:16.920 --> 00:54:20.822
Actually, it's not all about
the dresses and crowns, Carter.


00:54:20.891 --> 00:54:24.088
My mother told me that my father
never called himself king.


00:54:24.161 --> 00:54:27.597
To our people, he was father,
brother and friend.


00:54:29.767 --> 00:54:33.100
I hope to be like him
when I am Queen of Costa Luna.


00:54:33.804 --> 00:54:36.500
-Father, brother...
-No!


00:54:37.274 --> 00:54:39.435
I want to make a difference.


00:54:39.510 --> 00:54:41.603
To do something more important
with your life?


00:54:41.679 --> 00:54:42.737
Yes.


00:54:46.784 --> 00:54:50.015
You know, you're different
than I thought a princess would be.


00:54:50.087 --> 00:54:52.555
I hope that is a good thing.


00:54:52.623 --> 00:54:54.022
Yeah, it is.


00:54:55.025 --> 00:54:57.516
Thank you for helping me today.


00:54:57.594 --> 00:55:00.722
A princess is never sure
who her true friend is.


00:55:01.498 --> 00:55:03.125
Today, I am sure.


00:55:03.801 --> 00:55:05.029
Me, too.


00:55:15.813 --> 00:55:19.579
I'll give myself this one and this one,


00:55:20.050 --> 00:55:22.541
for bravery and honor.


00:55:22.619 --> 00:55:24.519
A thief has no honor.


00:55:24.588 --> 00:55:26.556
Sophia! Come in, come in, come in.


00:55:26.623 --> 00:55:30.457
We have a great deal to discuss.
Do you think it's too much?


00:55:31.028 --> 00:55:34.964
I want to look my best when I announce
my engagement today.


00:55:35.466 --> 00:55:39.061
Who could be so unfortunate
as to become your bride?


00:55:39.603 --> 00:55:42.163
Well, as a matter of fact,


00:55:43.674 --> 00:55:46.939
she is standing right here in this room.


00:55:48.912 --> 00:55:51.938
That's ridiculous.
I will never marry you. Ever.


00:55:52.015 --> 00:55:54.848
Of course you won't.


00:55:54.918 --> 00:55:57.216
But Rosalinda will not know this.


00:55:57.287 --> 00:56:01.485
She will see the announcement,
assume you are doing it to protect her,


00:56:01.692 --> 00:56:04.354
and come racing back
to her mother's side


00:56:04.428 --> 00:56:07.022
just in time to join you in exile.


00:56:07.097 --> 00:56:09.031
The people of Costa Luna
will never accept that.


00:56:09.099 --> 00:56:12.466
The same was said for the people
of Costa Estrella 20 years ago,


00:56:12.536 --> 00:56:14.595
and look what happened.


00:56:14.838 --> 00:56:15.827
Hmm.


00:56:16.073 --> 00:56:17.904
Take her back to her cell.


00:56:17.975 --> 00:56:21.274
Oh, and bring me
my hair and makeup team.


00:56:21.345 --> 00:56:24.542
We must touch up this gray
before I go on camera.


00:56:26.383 --> 00:56:27.509
Yeah.


00:56:28.819 --> 00:56:30.013
Sorry.


00:56:35.459 --> 00:56:36.824
Wait,
where's everyone going?


00:56:36.894 --> 00:56:38.794
Good morning, students.


00:56:38.862 --> 00:56:40.124
The votes
for your three homecoming...


00:56:40.197 --> 00:56:41.221
We must hurry, Carter.


00:56:41.298 --> 00:56:43.163
Okay, you're way too
into this princess thing.


00:56:43.233 --> 00:56:45.428
Now,
I'd like to announce the winners.


00:56:46.203 --> 00:56:50.162
And your princesses are
Chelsea Barnes!


00:56:56.580 --> 00:56:59.413
Thank you! Thank you!


00:56:59.783 --> 00:57:01.250
Carter Mason!


00:57:04.054 --> 00:57:05.578
"Carter Mason."


00:57:08.592 --> 00:57:11.925
And your third and final princess is


00:57:13.730 --> 00:57:15.425
Rosie Gonzalez!


00:57:24.808 --> 00:57:27.072
Thank you. Thank you.


00:57:32.249 --> 00:57:34.479
-What happened?
-I don't know!


00:57:34.685 --> 00:57:36.482
We texted everyone in the school.


00:57:36.553 --> 00:57:38.748
They were supposed to vote
for Carter instead of Rosie,


00:57:38.822 --> 00:57:40.653
not Carter and Rosie.


00:57:41.892 --> 00:57:44.827
-This is all your fault.
-How is it my fault?


00:57:45.229 --> 00:57:48.790
If you were more popular,
you'd be the princess, not her.


00:57:54.071 --> 00:57:55.595
I am popular!


00:58:01.411 --> 00:58:04.608
This is not good, okay?
Me being a princess is not normal.


00:58:04.681 --> 00:58:06.080
Hey, there.


00:58:07.384 --> 00:58:09.375
Hey, Rosie, can I talk to you?


00:58:09.453 --> 00:58:11.182
-Me?
-Her?


00:58:11.255 --> 00:58:12.279
Yeah.


00:58:12.356 --> 00:58:15.792
So, you know there's the homecoming
dance and everything, and...


00:58:15.859 --> 00:58:18.157
Will you go to the dance
with me, Rosie?


00:58:18.228 --> 00:58:19.991
-Me?
-Her?


00:58:20.063 --> 00:58:22.930
Yeah. I want you to be my date
for the dance.


00:58:23.000 --> 00:58:27.937
Donny, that is very kind of you, but no.


00:58:28.238 --> 00:58:29.705
Will you excuse me?


00:58:30.173 --> 00:58:31.231
Uh...


00:58:31.575 --> 00:58:32.701
Sure.


00:58:35.279 --> 00:58:38.612
That was the most humiliating thing
that has ever happened to me.


00:58:38.682 --> 00:58:41.048
And I've been humiliated a lot.


00:58:42.452 --> 00:58:46.252
What was I thinking? A guy like Donny
would never go out with me.


00:58:46.323 --> 00:58:48.518
Then he is not worthy of you.


00:58:50.027 --> 00:58:53.087
Yeah, you can say that
'cause you're all high and royal.


00:58:53.163 --> 00:58:56.257
-But I'm just a girl who sells bait.
-No.


00:58:57.434 --> 00:59:00.801
You are so much more.
You are a princess now.


00:59:01.438 --> 00:59:04.373
Yeah. Trust me, I am not a princess.


00:59:04.441 --> 00:59:05.965
Yes, you are.


00:59:06.343 --> 00:59:08.743
You just do not feel like one yet.


00:59:08.812 --> 00:59:12.612
When I came here, you taught me
how to act normal, not royal.


00:59:14.084 --> 00:59:16.382
Now it is my turn to teach you.


00:59:17.020 --> 00:59:20.080
You think that being a princess
is superficial.


00:59:20.157 --> 00:59:21.215
Yeah, I guess.


00:59:21.291 --> 00:59:24.590
That it is about what you wear,
and how you look.


00:59:25.996 --> 00:59:28.590
Well, it is a little bit
about how you look.


00:59:28.665 --> 00:59:30.724
But more importantly,


00:59:30.801 --> 00:59:33.793
it is about what you have to offer
the world and who you are inside.


00:59:38.842 --> 00:59:41.606
Come on, Carter.
Let's go find your inner princess.


00:59:54.925 --> 00:59:57.758
You come from here
I come from there


00:59:57.828 --> 01:00:00.991
You rock out in your room
I'd like a world premiere


01:00:01.064 --> 01:00:05.000
We're more alike
than anybody could ever tell


01:00:05.068 --> 01:00:06.399
Ever tell


01:00:07.137 --> 01:00:10.163
Friday we're cool
Monday we're freaks


01:00:10.240 --> 01:00:12.970
Sometimes we rule
Sometimes we can't even speak


01:00:13.043 --> 01:00:16.843
But we kick it up
Let loose and LOL


01:00:16.913 --> 01:00:18.073
LOL


01:00:18.148 --> 01:00:22.517
It may seem cliched for me
to want to say that you're not alone


01:00:22.586 --> 01:00:23.780
Not alone


01:00:23.854 --> 01:00:28.985
And you can call me uncool
But it's a simple fact I got your back


01:00:29.059 --> 01:00:30.219
Yeah, yeah, yeah


01:00:30.293 --> 01:00:33.694
'Cause we're one and the same


01:00:33.764 --> 01:00:36.699
We're anything but ordinary


01:00:36.767 --> 01:00:39.702
One and the same


01:00:39.770 --> 01:00:42.671
I think we're almost legendary


01:00:42.739 --> 01:00:45.606
You and me, the perfect team


01:00:45.675 --> 01:00:47.870
Chasing down the dream


01:00:47.944 --> 01:00:50.845
We're one and the same


01:00:54.217 --> 01:00:57.209
One and the same


01:00:57.287 --> 01:01:00.279
We're anything but ordinary


01:01:00.357 --> 01:01:03.326
One and the same


01:01:03.393 --> 01:01:06.328
I think we're almost legendary


01:01:06.396 --> 01:01:09.331
You and me, the perfect team


01:01:09.399 --> 01:01:11.458
Shaking up the scene


01:01:11.535 --> 01:01:14.595
We're one and the same


01:01:18.608 --> 01:01:21.133
You're just so good with everybody.


01:01:21.211 --> 01:01:24.874
Kids, old people,
you're probably even good with dogs.


01:01:25.215 --> 01:01:26.682
That is true.


01:01:27.250 --> 01:01:29.718
You're so much more generous
than I thought you'd be.


01:01:29.786 --> 01:01:32.380
It is a princess's job to help people.


01:01:33.690 --> 01:01:36.215
I guess I never really thought about


01:01:36.293 --> 01:01:38.318
what it really means to be a princess.


01:01:39.529 --> 01:01:41.520
Like this.


01:01:42.099 --> 01:01:44.260
I can't believe
you actually have to do this.


01:01:44.334 --> 01:01:45.995
Oh, no, you don't.


01:01:46.970 --> 01:01:49.495
-Wait, then, why am I doing it?
-Because it is funny.


01:01:49.573 --> 01:01:51.473
What? I hate you!


01:01:51.975 --> 01:01:53.943
-You do?
-No, no, no. No.


01:01:54.010 --> 01:01:56.535
No, I didn't mean it that way.
I didn't mean "l hate you" I hate you.


01:01:56.613 --> 01:01:59.707
I meant "l hate you," like,
you're my best friend.


01:01:59.783 --> 01:02:00.807
Oh!


01:02:00.884 --> 01:02:02.545
Well, then, I hate you, too.


01:02:02.619 --> 01:02:04.610
And that dress is ugly.


01:02:04.688 --> 01:02:06.656
-lt is?
-No!


01:02:08.258 --> 01:02:11.193
It is beautiful. And so are you.


01:02:12.629 --> 01:02:13.755
Look.


01:02:18.802 --> 01:02:21.566
You're becoming a princess
on the inside.


01:02:21.638 --> 01:02:23.970
And now you look like one, too.


01:02:32.816 --> 01:02:36.809
Excuse me, I have this lame reading
assignment for Spanish class.


01:02:36.887 --> 01:02:39.082
Do you think that you have
something that's really easy


01:02:39.156 --> 01:02:41.056
with lots of pictures?


01:02:46.163 --> 01:02:48.290
Oh! Cool.


01:03:08.285 --> 01:03:12.278
"Princess Rosalinda"? No way!


01:03:26.670 --> 01:03:28.467
It's Mason. What's going on?


01:03:28.538 --> 01:03:30.369
General Kane's
announcement of his engagement


01:03:30.440 --> 01:03:32.374
to dona Sophia Montoya


01:03:32.442 --> 01:03:35.843
has popped up
in several tabloid magazines.


01:03:35.912 --> 01:03:37.675
The story is contained so far,


01:03:37.747 --> 01:03:40.944
but I would be lying to say
I was not concerned.


01:03:41.017 --> 01:03:42.644
She'd never agree to marry him.


01:03:42.719 --> 01:03:45.119
I was not suggesting
she would, Major.


01:03:45.188 --> 01:03:47.588
General Kane's doing this
to draw Rosalinda out.


01:03:47.657 --> 01:03:50.387
He knows she won't allow her mother
to be forced into marriage.


01:03:50.460 --> 01:03:51.620
Absolutely.


01:03:51.695 --> 01:03:55.461
So, it is imperative
that we keep this from Rosalinda.


01:03:55.732 --> 01:03:57.495
Yes, ma'am. I agree.


01:03:57.567 --> 01:03:59.125
Major, has she made any enemies?


01:03:59.202 --> 01:04:02.262
Anyone who might want
to expose her identity?


01:04:02.339 --> 01:04:03.499
Not that I know of.


01:04:05.809 --> 01:04:08.607
Let's move that throne here.


01:04:09.212 --> 01:04:11.578
No. No, actually, there.


01:04:13.516 --> 01:04:15.950
Oh, I know. Up there.


01:04:19.022 --> 01:04:21.081
And let's hang some lights
directly on it.


01:04:21.157 --> 01:04:23.148
That might be too harsh
on my skin tone.


01:04:23.226 --> 01:04:25.126
We should hire a lighting designer.


01:04:25.195 --> 01:04:28.756
The budget's gone, Chelsea.
What you see is what you get.


01:04:28.898 --> 01:04:32.356
Okay, okay. I know!


01:04:32.469 --> 01:04:34.869
A follow-spot just on me.


01:04:34.938 --> 01:04:37.771
Maybe light pink,
or golden like the sun.


01:04:38.475 --> 01:04:40.272
It's great to be queen.


01:04:40.744 --> 01:04:43.872
You're not queen yet. Carter could win,


01:04:43.947 --> 01:04:46.108
-or Rosie.
-Can it, Muffy.


01:04:46.316 --> 01:04:49.183
-My name's Margaret.
-Not anymore.


01:04:51.655 --> 01:04:54.146
-Hey, Chels.
-Don't call me that.


01:04:54.224 --> 01:04:56.818
You lost that right when you lost
your princess crown to Bait Girl


01:04:56.893 --> 01:04:59.327
and her strangely formal cousin.


01:04:59.396 --> 01:05:03.025
Well, what if we could get Rosie
to drop out of homecoming altogether?


01:05:03.099 --> 01:05:05.795
-She would never do that.
-She might.


01:05:05.869 --> 01:05:10.033
She's not who she says she is.
She's Princesa Rosalinda.


01:05:12.609 --> 01:05:14.270
It's in Spanish.


01:05:15.478 --> 01:05:18.345
-What does the article say?
-I'm not sure.


01:05:18.648 --> 01:05:22.379
What? I'm pretty, not smart.
Okay, let me try.


01:05:24.754 --> 01:05:27.052
It's about Rosie and her mom.


01:05:27.891 --> 01:05:31.520
One of them has fled the country
and one of them is in prison


01:05:31.594 --> 01:05:32.822
or a paper bag.


01:05:32.896 --> 01:05:34.591
I get those two mixed up.


01:05:34.664 --> 01:05:37.531
No biggie. Good work, Brookie.


01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:39.158
Thanks, Chels.


01:05:40.937 --> 01:05:42.962
I have the perfect plan.


01:05:57.087 --> 01:06:00.352
-Hey, girls.
-Hi, Mr. Mason. Is Rosie home?


01:06:00.757 --> 01:06:02.987
-Maybe. What's up?
-Up?


01:06:03.059 --> 01:06:06.551
Well, we're planning
a little princess surprise for Carter.


01:06:06.629 --> 01:06:09.860
-To congratulate her.
-Yeah. It was Rosie's idea.


01:06:10.834 --> 01:06:12.961
She's in her room. Go on in.


01:06:30.453 --> 01:06:33.445
I've never heard of Costa Luna.
Have you, Brookie?


01:06:33.523 --> 01:06:34.990
No, Chels.


01:06:35.525 --> 01:06:37.015
I do not know
what you are talking about.


01:06:37.093 --> 01:06:40.654
We know all about you
and your mother. And the paper bag.


01:06:41.030 --> 01:06:43.931
-What?
-Poor Princess Rosalinda.


01:06:44.000 --> 01:06:46.195
Did you hear she's in hiding?


01:06:46.603 --> 01:06:50.198
-You do not understand.
-I understand that you lied to us.


01:06:50.273 --> 01:06:53.140
-Only to protect my mother.
-From the paper bag?


01:06:53.209 --> 01:06:54.335
No.


01:06:54.411 --> 01:06:57.471
Look, I will give you a reward
for keeping my secret.


01:06:57.714 --> 01:07:00.239
-We know you will.
-You do?


01:07:00.984 --> 01:07:03.509
And we already have it picked out.


01:07:03.586 --> 01:07:06.214
-I don't understand.
-Yeah, me either.


01:07:07.791 --> 01:07:09.884
You're gonna turn in
your crown, Princess.


01:07:09.959 --> 01:07:13.520
You're going to tell everyone
that there is, and only will be,


01:07:13.596 --> 01:07:16.793
one true homecoming queen,
and that's me.


01:07:16.866 --> 01:07:18.595
-That's good.
-Fine.


01:07:19.068 --> 01:07:21.229
You may take my crown,


01:07:21.771 --> 01:07:25.901
but you will not take Carter's.
She's no threat to you, Chelsea.


01:07:27.644 --> 01:07:28.770
Fine.


01:07:28.845 --> 01:07:31.678
Let Bait Girl
play princess for one night.


01:07:32.982 --> 01:07:34.643
She just won't look like one.


01:07:52.869 --> 01:07:54.803
 Have fun at the dance!


01:08:10.920 --> 01:08:13.548
Look at what Chelsea and Brooke...


01:08:13.623 --> 01:08:15.921
-What's wrong?
-I have to leave, Carter.


01:08:15.992 --> 01:08:17.721
Leave? Leave where?


01:08:18.027 --> 01:08:19.790
Back to my country.


01:08:28.972 --> 01:08:32.066
General Kane is forcing my mother
into marriage.


01:08:32.575 --> 01:08:35.772
-Father's never gonna let you go back.
-He'll never know.


01:08:35.845 --> 01:08:38.006
Yeah, but I know. And I'm not gonna
let you go back, either.


01:08:38.081 --> 01:08:40.140
Carter, you have to stay out of this.


01:08:40.216 --> 01:08:41.649
I have a duty to my people.


01:08:41.718 --> 01:08:45.051
And this is something
that you'll never understand.


01:08:46.356 --> 01:08:48.984
I've loved living here in Louisiana.


01:08:49.893 --> 01:08:53.090
And I wish my life could be like this
every day.


01:08:53.930 --> 01:08:55.921
But this is not reality.


01:08:56.733 --> 01:09:01.636
I mean, you think
my life as a princess is some fairy tale?


01:09:04.440 --> 01:09:06.635
This here is a fairy tale!


01:09:07.877 --> 01:09:10.175
And I cannot hide here anymore.


01:09:10.947 --> 01:09:13.438
Soon I will be Queen of Costa Luna.


01:09:15.585 --> 01:09:17.382
My country needs me.


01:09:18.388 --> 01:09:21.653
You're right. They do need you.


01:09:23.426 --> 01:09:26.554
They need you to lead them,
and to protect them.


01:09:27.964 --> 01:09:29.659
And that's something
you can't do from jail,


01:09:29.732 --> 01:09:33.862
which is exactly where you'll end up
if you go back to Costa Luna.


01:09:42.512 --> 01:09:44.844
No way am I letting this happen.


01:09:57.527 --> 01:10:00.052
Hola, this is Elegante. Who is this?


01:10:00.129 --> 01:10:01.323
That's not important.


01:10:01.397 --> 01:10:03.661
All that matters
is I'm a friend of Princess Rosalinda,


01:10:03.733 --> 01:10:05.860
and she's about to make
a very big mistake.


01:10:05.935 --> 01:10:09.393
My princesa? What mistake is this?


01:10:09.472 --> 01:10:11.372
 She wants to come home.


01:10:11.708 --> 01:10:13.801
No, no, no, no, no, she must not.


01:10:15.078 --> 01:10:16.477
It's too dangerous.


01:10:16.980 --> 01:10:19.608
I know. But I have a plan.


01:10:20.183 --> 01:10:22.378
And I'm gonna need you
to listen very carefully.


01:10:23.219 --> 01:10:26.552
I will do anything for the Princesa.
Anything.


01:10:27.190 --> 01:10:30.284
Okay, to start with,
I'm gonna need two dresses.


01:10:40.069 --> 01:10:41.331
You okay?


01:10:41.871 --> 01:10:44.066
I'm going to miss this place.


01:10:45.508 --> 01:10:47.203
I'm going to miss you, Carter.


01:10:47.276 --> 01:10:51.178
I can't believe I'm saying this,
but I'm going to miss you, too.


01:10:55.284 --> 01:10:58.617
Rosie, can you do me
a big favor before you go?


01:10:59.389 --> 01:11:00.413
Anything.


01:11:00.490 --> 01:11:03.482
You said it is a princess' job
to help others.


01:11:04.260 --> 01:11:05.420
It is.


01:11:05.628 --> 01:11:07.596
Well, the dance is on Friday night,


01:11:07.664 --> 01:11:10.599
and there's some people
that I want to help.


01:11:10.933 --> 01:11:14.596
I want to make this night
special for them, for all of us.


01:11:15.171 --> 01:11:17.605
Will you please stay until then?


01:11:18.374 --> 01:11:20.035
For them, please.


01:11:46.202 --> 01:11:48.397
That's it,
keep your chin up.


01:11:48.905 --> 01:11:50.099
What in the...


01:11:50.173 --> 01:11:53.939
Okay, stay there,
that's perfect. Very good.


01:11:55.344 --> 01:11:57.312
-Morning, Dad.
-Morning. What the...


01:11:57.380 --> 01:11:58.642
What are you girls up to?


01:11:58.715 --> 01:12:00.945
Just having some friends over
from school. Is that okay?


01:12:01.017 --> 01:12:03.110
Yeah, yeah. It's fine. What's in the box?


01:12:03.186 --> 01:12:05.313
Homecoming stuff. No biggie.


01:12:12.061 --> 01:12:13.221
Hmm.


01:12:15.164 --> 01:12:18.964
And you are sure about this
homecoming dance, Senor Elegante?


01:12:19.235 --> 01:12:20.600
Absolutely.


01:12:21.137 --> 01:12:24.504
I feel, in one way,
I'm betraying my queen,


01:12:24.574 --> 01:12:27.168
but I thought
you should know, General.


01:12:27.243 --> 01:12:30.269
It's for the good of Costa Luna.


01:12:30.947 --> 01:12:34.348
You did the right thing
by coming to me, senor.


01:12:34.550 --> 01:12:36.040
Fuel the jet!


01:12:36.519 --> 01:12:39.147
Tell the pilot
we will be flying to Louisiana.


01:12:45.128 --> 01:12:48.461
A lovely color. Lovely indeed.


01:12:48.998 --> 01:12:50.863
Caribbean blue, General.


01:12:50.933 --> 01:12:54.391
To complement
Princess Rosalinda's skin tone.


01:12:55.671 --> 01:12:59.004
Well, back to work.
You have a dress to finish.


01:13:02.445 --> 01:13:04.003
Two, actually.


01:13:14.457 --> 01:13:15.617
Where did you get them?


01:13:15.691 --> 01:13:18.683
Well, you said to call Mr. Elegante
if I had an emergency.


01:13:18.761 --> 01:13:20.524
And I think
that this is a fashion emergency.


01:13:20.596 --> 01:13:24.327
-Carter, you are brilliant.
-This one is yours.


01:13:25.201 --> 01:13:27.465
He says you look best in pink.


01:13:27.904 --> 01:13:30.964
And this one is mine.
It's Caribbean blue.


01:13:33.209 --> 01:13:36.770
Thank you, Carter.
This is a night I'll always remember.


01:13:40.116 --> 01:13:41.447
I hope so.


01:13:43.052 --> 01:13:45.543
Are you guys ready?
'Cause it's getting kind of late.


01:13:45.621 --> 01:13:47.054
Come on in, girls.


01:13:47.123 --> 01:13:50.320
Helen's House of Beauty
is open for business.


01:13:57.633 --> 01:13:58.793
Okay.


01:14:00.336 --> 01:14:02.531
Oh, this is a great color on you.


01:14:16.652 --> 01:14:18.381
How do I look, Dad?


01:14:18.988 --> 01:14:21.047
I think we have a problem.


01:14:22.325 --> 01:14:24.953
I may have to stop calling you "pal."


01:14:30.800 --> 01:14:33.325
All right, I gotta grab this.
You girls gonna be okay?


01:14:33.402 --> 01:14:35.768
-Yeah, we'll be fine. Go ahead.
-You sure?


01:14:35.838 --> 01:14:37.328
Of course. We're not kids.


01:14:37.406 --> 01:14:39.772
All right. Well, have a good time.
And be careful.


01:14:40.743 --> 01:14:42.267
-Mason.
-Helen.


01:14:42.778 --> 01:14:44.769
All right, Your Highnesses.


01:14:44.847 --> 01:14:48.044
Time's a-wasting.
The dance starts in 1 0 minutes.


01:15:37.767 --> 01:15:40.827
Masks? No one said anything
about masks.


01:15:43.973 --> 01:15:45.338
Come on!


01:15:50.980 --> 01:15:53.312
Hey! Hey!


01:15:54.183 --> 01:15:57.482
I'm stuck!
Open the door, Donny. Hello?


01:15:58.955 --> 01:16:00.047
Donny. Donny!


01:16:09.598 --> 01:16:11.395
Come here, come here.


01:16:14.170 --> 01:16:16.968
-You okay?
-Get off!


01:16:44.000 --> 01:16:47.128
Okay, freshman,
I think I can take it from here.


01:16:57.013 --> 01:16:59.607
-No.
-Carter, what's the problem?


01:16:59.882 --> 01:17:02.578
I thought we had,
you know, something.


01:17:02.651 --> 01:17:05.245
-Actually, we don't.
-Okay, what's up?


01:17:05.821 --> 01:17:08.551
Isn't this what you've been waiting
for since, like, third grade?


01:17:08.624 --> 01:17:12.560
Before I put on this dress,
you couldn't even remember my name.


01:17:14.063 --> 01:17:17.897
I might be a princess tonight,
but I'll always be Bait Girl.


01:17:18.234 --> 01:17:20.134
And I'm proud of that.


01:17:21.637 --> 01:17:24.265
Carter, you're making a big mistake.


01:17:26.042 --> 01:17:28.567
No, Donny. I don't think I am.


01:17:35.017 --> 01:17:36.746
You deserve better than him, Carter.


01:17:36.819 --> 01:17:39.982
I know.
Too bad it took this long to realize it.


01:17:41.023 --> 01:17:42.183
Guys!


01:17:53.536 --> 01:17:54.969
What happened to you?


01:17:55.037 --> 01:17:56.766
Shut up and fix me.


01:17:56.872 --> 01:17:58.635
-Did you get me a crown?
-Who cares?


01:17:58.707 --> 01:18:00.538
In a few minutes,
it won't matter anyways.


01:18:00.609 --> 01:18:03.635
I'll be named queen
and this will all be over.


01:18:04.246 --> 01:18:06.544
I thought we were in this together.


01:18:06.615 --> 01:18:09.243
We are. Lip gloss.


01:18:09.585 --> 01:18:10.643
No.


01:18:10.719 --> 01:18:12.619
-What?
-I said no.


01:18:12.688 --> 01:18:14.349
You can't use my lip gloss anymore.


01:18:14.423 --> 01:18:16.914
But I have to look pretty. I'm a princess.


01:18:16.992 --> 01:18:18.926
Yeah, a terrible one.


01:18:18.994 --> 01:18:22.054
A princess is supposed to be
a girl of exemplary character,


01:18:22.131 --> 01:18:24.065
a role model. But you,


01:18:24.133 --> 01:18:27.591
you're not even kind,
honest or charitable in any way.


01:18:28.304 --> 01:18:30.499
You're not even nice.


01:18:30.573 --> 01:18:33.542
I don't think
I want to be your friend anymore.


01:18:33.676 --> 01:18:36.406
-Brookie...
-Don't call me that.


01:18:41.317 --> 01:18:45.413
Carter, Rosie,
I just wanted to thank you for tonight.


01:18:46.088 --> 01:18:50.923
I never thought I could look beautiful.
Or feel beautiful, for that matter.


01:18:51.227 --> 01:18:52.922
Margaret, you are beautiful.


01:18:54.530 --> 01:18:57.499
And thanks for not calling me Muffy.


01:18:57.833 --> 01:18:59.391
No problem.


01:19:00.769 --> 01:19:03.329
I love this song! Let's go dance!


01:19:03.405 --> 01:19:05.430
Well, why don't you two go ahead?
Be princesses.


01:19:05.508 --> 01:19:06.805
Okay!


01:19:13.282 --> 01:19:15.477
There you are! Finally!


01:19:15.551 --> 01:19:16.882
You don't understand, miss.


01:19:16.952 --> 01:19:20.115
-I'm the...
-Security. I know. You're late.


01:19:20.689 --> 01:19:23.658
And what is with the uniforms?


01:19:23.726 --> 01:19:26.251
No one's wearing berets this year.


01:19:26.328 --> 01:19:29.354
Just stay out here and make sure
no one gets in that dance,


01:19:29.431 --> 01:19:32.662
unless they're students
from Lake Monroe. Got it?


01:19:34.603 --> 01:19:37.936
Got it. Enjoy your evening.


01:19:51.820 --> 01:19:53.344
Okay, everybody, he's about to
announce the winner.


01:19:53.422 --> 01:19:56.289
Let's put on our masks.


01:20:10.439 --> 01:20:12.339
Princesses everywhere.


01:20:17.246 --> 01:20:21.478
Caribbean blue. Beautiful indeed.


01:20:25.020 --> 01:20:29.116
Come with me now, Princesa,
and no harm will come to your friends.


01:20:34.530 --> 01:20:38.398
Can I have your attention, please?
I hold here in my hand


01:20:38.467 --> 01:20:43.404
the name of our 2008
Lake Monroe Homecoming Queen.


01:20:45.074 --> 01:20:46.803
And the winner is


01:20:48.844 --> 01:20:51.142
Princess Rosie Gonzalez.


01:20:53.716 --> 01:20:55.707
Rosie, are you out there?


01:21:20.409 --> 01:21:21.774
Thank you.


01:21:22.411 --> 01:21:25.972
Since I've been here,
I've learned many wonderful things.


01:21:26.048 --> 01:21:27.709
Most importantly,


01:21:29.785 --> 01:21:35.052
I've learned about friendship
and loyalty and trust.


01:21:36.292 --> 01:21:39.625
And that those are not things
that are just given,


01:21:40.763 --> 01:21:42.788
but things we must earn.


01:21:44.566 --> 01:21:47.694
So I want to thank Carter Mason


01:21:48.704 --> 01:21:50.934
for teaching me these things.


01:21:53.075 --> 01:21:55.066
And for being my friend.


01:21:57.813 --> 01:22:00.407
Carter, where are you?


01:22:18.400 --> 01:22:20.868
That was so beautiful, Rosie.


01:22:20.936 --> 01:22:23.632
Thank you. But I need to find Carter.


01:22:34.350 --> 01:22:36.910
Hold it right there, Princess.


01:22:36.985 --> 01:22:39.146
My crown. Hand it over.


01:22:39.655 --> 01:22:41.953
-Chelsea, please...
-You're not going anywhere


01:22:42.024 --> 01:22:43.958
until I get that crown.


01:22:48.230 --> 01:22:49.788
No!


01:22:51.834 --> 01:22:52.994
Sorry.


01:22:53.068 --> 01:22:55.502
I am so getting you back for this!


01:22:59.808 --> 01:23:01.275
General Kane!


01:23:06.315 --> 01:23:11.048
Well, it appears as if
everyone wants to be a princess.


01:23:11.120 --> 01:23:14.487
Unfortunately, it is time
for the masquerade to end.


01:23:15.124 --> 01:23:18.389
What are you doing?
The plan was working perfectly.


01:23:18.594 --> 01:23:20.721
This was a very brave plan.


01:23:21.797 --> 01:23:23.958
But this is my fight, not yours.


01:23:24.032 --> 01:23:26.762
-You don't have to go with them.
-Enough!


01:23:27.336 --> 01:23:30.305
As the Princesa
so eloquently pointed out,


01:23:31.240 --> 01:23:33.174
this is not your fight.


01:23:47.389 --> 01:23:48.856
General Kane.


01:23:49.124 --> 01:23:51.854
-Good to see you again.
-What is the meaning of this?


01:23:51.927 --> 01:23:53.417
You are interfering
with official business


01:23:53.495 --> 01:23:54.962
of the sovereign land of Costa Luna.


01:23:55.030 --> 01:23:58.659
Maybe this will fly in your country,
but, here, it's called kidnapping.


01:23:58.734 --> 01:24:02.363
We're turning you over
to the international authorities.


01:24:03.172 --> 01:24:05.333
-Get him.
-No, let me.


01:24:05.774 --> 01:24:07.173
I'm going to enjoy this.


01:24:21.924 --> 01:24:25.519
How does it feel to be brought to justice
by a 16-year-old girl, General?


01:24:25.594 --> 01:24:27.118
Not so hot.


01:24:33.836 --> 01:24:36.634
I can't believe you would do this for me.


01:24:37.906 --> 01:24:39.965
That's what princesses do.


01:24:40.342 --> 01:24:42.242
They do it for each other.


01:24:42.311 --> 01:24:45.405
And you are truly a princess now,
Carter Mason.


01:24:46.715 --> 01:24:48.910
You rightfully deserve this.


01:24:54.590 --> 01:24:57.855
Hold it! Nobody moves!


01:24:58.527 --> 01:25:00.358
Nobody goes anywhere.


01:25:02.698 --> 01:25:04.256
I'll take that.


01:25:08.871 --> 01:25:11.237
Let her go.
She needs it way more than I do.


01:25:11.306 --> 01:25:12.603
All right. Come on. Hey, guard.


01:25:15.277 --> 01:25:16.710
You got him?


01:25:17.546 --> 01:25:20.538
Oh, I'm in so much trouble.


01:25:27.389 --> 01:25:29.619
What were you thinking, Carter?


01:25:29.691 --> 01:25:32.216
I was thinking I'd be perfect bait.


01:25:32.294 --> 01:25:34.455
Get it? I'm Bait Girl.


01:25:34.530 --> 01:25:35.724
Why didn't you just come to me?


01:25:35.797 --> 01:25:38.493
Dad, you would have never let me do it.


01:25:39.835 --> 01:25:43.066
-You're lucky I was here.
-I knew you would be.


01:25:44.106 --> 01:25:46.267
You're always there for me.


01:25:47.075 --> 01:25:50.340
You rescue princesses.
That's what you do.


01:25:52.681 --> 01:25:54.308
You and me, pal.


01:25:55.884 --> 01:25:57.476
You and me, Dad.


01:26:09.731 --> 01:26:11.858
I present to you


01:26:13.135 --> 01:26:17.094
Queen Rosalinda Marie Montoya Fiore


01:26:17.172 --> 01:26:18.969
of Costa Luna!


01:26:35.123 --> 01:26:37.489
Long live Queen Rosie!


01:26:41.229 --> 01:26:43.527
Long live Queen Rosie!


01:26:55.744 --> 01:26:59.111
You had your dreams, I had mine


01:26:59.715 --> 01:27:03.116
You had your fears, I was fine


01:27:03.518 --> 01:27:07.352
You showed me what I couldn't find


01:27:07.422 --> 01:27:10.414
When two different worlds collide


01:27:11.393 --> 01:27:17.127
When two different worlds collide


01:27:27.442 --> 01:27:30.206
Ladies, you're here. Excellent.


01:27:30.278 --> 01:27:31.836
Are you ready
for your next assignment?


01:27:31.913 --> 01:27:33.278
-I am.
-Me, too.


01:27:33.348 --> 01:27:34.906
But can we go somewhere
a little bit warmer?


01:27:34.983 --> 01:27:37.315
My feet are still frozen
from that walk through Helsinki.


01:27:41.556 --> 01:27:44.150
Carter, you can be such a princess.


01:27:44.660 --> 01:27:45.752
Something wrong with that?


01:27:45.827 --> 01:27:47.294
Door opening.

